# Zaytoon AI — root environment pointer
#
# There is intentionally NO root `.env`. The backend calls `load_dotenv()` from
# `backend/config.py` and must be launched with `backend/` as the working
# directory (see AGENTS.md, "Key quirks"), so it reads exactly one file:
#
#     backend/.env
#
# The real template — with the zero-cost model policy, the permission tiers and
# the workspace setting — lives at:
#
#     backend/.env.example
#
# A previous root `.env.example` existed and was actively misleading: it set
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=qwen/qwen2.5-7b-instruct, which is neither in the
# ALLOWED_FREE_MODELS allow-list nor in a `:free` form, so a user who copied it
# would get a NonFreeModelError at startup and a backend that could not answer.
# Do not reintroduce a second .env template.
#
# Quick start:
#     cd backend
#     copy .env.example .env        # then set OPENROUTER_API_KEY
#
# Desktop shell variables (ZAYTOON_*) are read directly from the environment by
# desktop/app/config.py; see desktop/app/config.py for the full list.
